                "text": "Different denominator. A reporting and ERP case is measured per report and per field hour, because those are the units of contractor cost. A digital twin case is measured per asset and per turnaround, because the value sits in inspection planning and remaining-life decisions across many years of history. They are complementary but not interchangeable — see digital twin vs IDMS for where that boundary falls."
